"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2935,"Narrated to us 'Abdul-Jabbar ibnul-'Ala', narrated to us Sufyan, who said: I heard 'Abdur-Rahman ibnul-Qasim informing, on the authority of his father, on the authority of 'Aishah (RA), who said:
""We went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). She said: 'I menstruated, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me while I was weeping. He said: ""What is the matter with you? Are you experiencing respiratory distress?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""This is something that Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam. So do what the pilgrims do, except that you should not perform Tawaf around the House.""'""

**CHAPTER:**"
